WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, Amy, you directed
"Wine Country".

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:07.207
That was with your closest "SNL"
friends, outside of yours truly.

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:09.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I'm wondering
what the experience was like

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:11.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
working with this young,
talented cast --

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:15.348 size:78% position:39%
I'll show it again --
and your old friends.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.883 line:92%
-Oh, look at those cuties.

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:20.320
Well, I really, really had
great experiences on both.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:23.523
I think with "Wine Country,"
it was a little more sisterly.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:28.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I would guess
maybe in this film, "Moxie,"

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:31.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
I perhaps was
a little bit more maternal

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:35.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I don't know.
"Moxie," it's more dramatic.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:38.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it kind of deals
with some deeper issues,

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:42.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
so there was a lot of
sensitive subject matter

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:44.444 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and very thoughtful --

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:48.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
very thoughtful preparatio
and discussions from the cast.

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:52.385
In "Wine Country," I don't think
anyone even read the script.

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:54.087 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:55.055 line:92%
-Now, did they admit to you,

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:57.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
or would it be, over the cours
of the day, it would

00:00:57.123 --> 00:01:00.427
slowly dawn on you that none
of them had read the script?

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:01.728 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Realize...

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.863
You know,
an actress would come up and go,

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:06.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, so we're
supposed to be friends?"

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:09.069 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:11.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Speaking of working
with friends, you and Am--

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:15.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
Excuse me. You and Tina
are hosting the Golden Globes.

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.444 line:92%
How's prep for the Globes going?

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:21.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So good, Seth.
The prep is going so good.

00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:23.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
We just have
a few final questions,

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:29.789 size:78% position:39%
which is, when, how,
why, where, and what.

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:30.523 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Great.

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:32.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just those --
That's all we need to find out

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we're going to
figure it out.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:38.932
-I think it will be a tonic fo
all of us to see the two of yo

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:41.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
in whatever arena
it ends up being.

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:43.169 line:92%
I'm looking forward to it.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.905 line:92%
I know you use time like thi

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:48.842 size:84% position:42%
where a lot of people
are watching television

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:50.110 line:92%
because you can't go out as much

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:52.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
to catch up on the latest
in television.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-The most groundbreaking -

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.716 line:92%
The TV, the films of today

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:58.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
What have you been watchin
the most?

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.620
-Well, I've been watching
this amazing new show.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:03.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
I cannot recommend it highly
enough. Which is "E.R."

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:07.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I've been watching it
from top to bottom.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:11.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is my third time throug
in my lifetime,

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:13.700 line:92%
but this is -- and I can't -

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.135 line:92%
I can't stop watching "E.R."

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:19.906
So now I'm into, like, the Wik
fandom of all the characters

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:22.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm spending all my time
just Googling, like,

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:25.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What happened to the surgeo
in season one?"

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:29.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Why did William H. Macy
not stay on 'E.R.'?"

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:35.054
"Was Eriq La Salle and Noah Wyle
actual friends?"

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:36.756 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Like, I'm just so deep.

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:40.026
And, Seth, you know, people like
to talk about the cool thing

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:43.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are on Netflix or on HBO,
and that's great.

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:48.401 line:92%
But Dr. Carter's journey..

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:50.270 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
is so good.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:53.740
And at one point,
he's saving people in the Congo.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.008 size:78% position:39% line:92%
This show is so good.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:57.577 size:84% position:42%
-I'm glad you're giving
Noah Wyle his credit.

00:02:57.577 --> 00:03:02.348
Because Clooney obviously,
Doug Ross, was everything.

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:04.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Clooney's the obvious reaso
why you --

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:10.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
You go for Clooney.
You stay for Noah Wyle.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.391 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:16.296
-Has Clooney's -- Has Clooney'
performance held up for you?

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:18.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did have a moment
recently in --

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:22.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know what month
it was -- where I realized

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:24.070 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I was maybe too lonely

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
and had been
quarantining too hard.

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:29.142
Because it was the middle of the
day, and I was in my pajamas

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:30.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was watching, like -
I don't know --

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:33.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
re-watching
season three, episode ten,

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:37.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
where Clooney saves a kid
that's stuck in a water pipe

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he lifts him up
out of the water.

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:43.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I stood up and pointed
at the TV, and I said,

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:45.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
"And that's when
he became a star!"

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:46.759 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:49.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
No one was home.
-You weren't wrong.

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:51.764 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-No. No. That was it.

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:55.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know,
I'm at a point now, Seth,

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:56.936 line:92%
where, look, we're very lucky.

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.137 size:81% position:41% line:92%
We have fancy friends.

00:03:58.137 --> 00:04:00.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sometimes -- I know you have
a lot of fancy friends.

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:02.842 line:92%
And you are my fancy friend.

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:05.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I have a friend
who kind of --

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:07.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, who knows
Julianna Margulies.

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:09.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I texted him,
and I was like --

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:11.517 size:81% position:41%
You know, I was trying
to set some intentions

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:14.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
for things so that I can
look forward to doing things

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.623 line:92%
once this lockdown is over

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:20.059
"Is there any way, maybe in th
summer or in the fall, when --

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:24.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, when things
get less stressful and scary

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:27.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I could meet
Julianna Margulies

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.735 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
at a restaurant?

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:30.470 line:92%
And ask her a list of question

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:33.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have about
Nurse Carol Hathaway,

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:35.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
her character that she playe
on 'E.R.' 20 years ago?"

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:40.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the friend was like,
"You know, um, I'll ask her.

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:41.981 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:44.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I have --
I just want her to know

00:04:44.284 --> 00:04:47.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I have a hard 50 question
waiting for her.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:51.624
-I -- Look, I'm going to mak
sure the next time she's her

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:53.359 line:92%
I lock down that date for you.

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:55.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh. That would be amazing
That would --

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:57.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you --
Have you ever watched "E.R."

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause you're acting like
you haven't.

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:03.770
-Amy, they weren't lying whe
they called it Must See TV

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:04.671 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-100%. 100%.

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:07.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I was shooting
"Wet Hot American Summer,"

00:05:07.807 --> 00:05:10.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
a little gem
that we shot, like, 1999 -

00:05:10.343 --> 00:05:13.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
before there were
cellphones, folks --

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:14.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
they used to have
these, like, TVs

00:05:14.614 --> 00:05:16.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you could wear
around your neck.

00:05:16.616 --> 00:05:21.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was the episode
when Carol Hathaway went -

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:23.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
Julianna Margulies
went back to Clooney,

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:26.592
and somebody was watching it
on TV, running around, crying.

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:28.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like,
"She went back to Clooney!

00:05:28.528 --> 00:05:30.930 line:92%
I mean, those were the days.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:31.564 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I remember --

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:35.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
I recently watched just
the last -- her last episode

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:37.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was that --- Is that the one
you're talking about

00:05:37.704 --> 00:05:40.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you see Clooney
at the waterside?

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:42.942 line:92%
-Yes, when she flies to Seattle.

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:45.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's like, "I have twins.
What am I doing?

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:50.350 size:75% position:38%
I mean, I love Luka,
but he's not for me.

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.585 size:81% position:41% line:92%
He's going to find..."

00:05:52.585 --> 00:05:54.454 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Preaching to the choir.

00:05:54.454 --> 00:05:55.955 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:55.955 --> 00:05:59.659
Well, I feel like we've done
a good job plugging a lot of

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:04.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
mid-to-late-'90s work
that took place in Chicago

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:05.498 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:09.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"E.R.," "The Matrix,"
and Amy Poehler.

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:10.002 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-I mean, when you --

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:12.905 size:78% position:39%
when you think of me,
you think of, like,

00:06:12.905 --> 00:06:15.108 size:88% position:44% line:92%
what's next, what's new.

00:06:15.108 --> 00:06:16.743 line:92%
-What's the next big thing

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:19.612
I want to finish by saying
thank you for being here

00:06:19.612 --> 00:06:22.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
and also that the third season
of "Making It" --

00:06:22.615 --> 00:06:26.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love you, Amy -- premieres
later this year on NBC.

00:06:26.319 --> 00:06:28.221 line:92%
And Amy's film "Moxie"...

00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:29.989 line:92%
-Bye. I'll see you at home

00:06:29.989 --> 00:06:30.823 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:30.823 --> 00:06:34.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
...releases on Netflix
March 3rd.

